into cv/sense.amni
namespace sense
lang amni
use companion

Recognition for the companion's camera senses: turns per-frame MediaPipe results into discrete events. All state lives in module-level fixed arrays (no growable arrays). Event codes: 1 enter, 2 leave, 3 wave, 4 hands_up, 5 clap, 6 point, 7 arms_crossed, 8 t_pose, 9 approach, 10 back_away, 11 thumbs_up, 12 thumbs_down, 13 peace, 14 love, 15 fist, 16 open_palm, 17 pointing_up, 18 smile, 19 surprise, 20 frown, 21 wink, 22 nod, 23 head_shake, 24 object. `NEV` = 25. `sense_name(code int) const byte[:]` returns those names ("?" otherwise).

Inputs to `sense_frame(t real, pose real[:], hands real[:], face real[:], objs real[:], ev i32[:]) int` (t in seconds, increasing): pose holds 33 image landmarks of 4 reals (x, y in 0..1 with y down, z, visibility), then pose[132] = 1 when a person is detected and pose[133] = image width / height. Points are used as (x·aspect, y). hands holds two (gesture, score) pairs with gesture 0 none, 1 Closed_Fist, 2 Open_Palm, 3 Pointing_Up, 4 Thumb_Down, 5 Thumb_Up, 6 Victory, 7 ILoveYou. face holds the 52 MediaPipe blendshapes in their standard order (0 _neutral, 1 browDownLeft, 2 browDownRight, 3 browInnerUp, 9 eyeBlinkLeft, 10 eyeBlinkRight, 21 eyeWideLeft, 22 eyeWideRight, 25 jawOpen, 30 mouthFrownLeft, 31 mouthFrownRight, 44 mouthSmileLeft, 45 mouthSmileRight, …), then face[52] = head yaw and face[53] = head pitch in radians, face[54] = 1 when a face is detected. objs holds up to 8 (class id, score) pairs, then objs[16] = how many. Events go to ev as (code, arg) pairs; return how many events (at most 17 per frame).

General rules. "Held for X" means the condition has been true on every frame for at least X seconds; it fires once per hold, and the condition must turn false before it can fire again. Every code has a 2.5 second cooldown after it fires, except open_palm (10 s), object (45 s per class) and enter/leave (none). A reversal detector tracks one value: it keeps the last extreme and the current direction, and counts a reversal (with its time) when the value moves more than a threshold away from the last extreme against the current direction; it fires when enough reversals fall inside a time window, then clears. Landmarks: nose 0, LS 11, RS 12, LE 13, RE 14, LW 15, RW 16, LH 23, RH 24. sw = distance between LS and RS. The elbow angle is the angle at the elbow between the shoulder and the wrist.

Presence: present means pose[132] > 0.5 and both shoulders have visibility > 0.5. enter fires when present has held for 0.5 s after at least 2.0 s absent (the start counts as absent); leave fires when absent has held for 2.5 s after an enter. While not present, reset every body rule's state below.

Body rules while present. wave (arg 0 for wrist 15, 1 for wrist 16): per side, active while the wrist is above its elbow (smaller y); a reversal detector on the wrist x with threshold 0.12·sw fires on 3 reversals within 1.7 s; when inactive clear that side. hands_up: both wrists above nose y - 0.15·sw, held 0.4 s. clap: d = |LW - RW| / sw; after d > 0.9 a clap counts when d < 0.3; fires on 2 claps within 1.5 s, then clears. t_pose: both elbow angles > 170 degrees, both |wrist y - shoulder y| < 0.35·sw and both |wrist x - shoulder x| > 1.4·sw, held 0.7 s. point (arg 1 when the wrist x is greater than its shoulder x, else 0): per side, elbow angle > 150 degrees, |wrist x - shoulder x| > 1.2·sw, |wrist y - shoulder y| < 0.7·sw, not in t_pose, held 0.5 s. arms_crossed: |LW - RE| < 0.7·sw and |RW - LE| < 0.7·sw, held 0.8 s. approach/back_away: a baseline b of sw, set to sw on enter and otherwise moved toward sw as an exponential average with a 3 second time constant; approach fires when sw > 1.3·b and back_away when sw < 0.75·b, and either resets b = sw.

Hand gesture rules: when either hand reports gesture g > 0 with score > 0.7, held 0.35 s, fire 15 for g 1, 16 for g 2, 17 for g 3, 12 for g 4, 11 for g 5, 13 for g 6, 14 for g 7; skip open_palm when a wave fired in the last 2 s.

Face rules while face[54] > 0.5 (otherwise reset them). smile: (bs44 + bs45)/2 > 0.55, held 0.7 s. surprise: bs25 > 0.45 and (bs3 > 0.4 or (bs21 + bs22)/2 > 0.35), held 0.25 s. frown: (((bs30 + bs31)/2 > 0.35 and (bs1 + bs2)/2 > 0.35) or (bs30 + bs31)/2 > 0.6) and not smiling, held 1.7 s. wink: (bs9 > 0.7 and bs10 < 0.25) or (bs10 > 0.7 and bs9 < 0.25); fires when the condition ends after lasting between 0.12 and 0.7 s. nod: reversal detector on pitch, threshold 0.07, 2 reversals within 1.2 s. head_shake: reversal detector on yaw, threshold 0.1, 2 reversals within 1.2 s.

Object rule: for each detection with score > 0.55 and class 1 to 79, a class counts as seen continuously while the gap between sightings stays under 0.5 s; object (arg = class id) fires when a class has been seen continuously for 0.7 s.

`sense_reset()` clears all state.
